(2018772, 274880, 40819, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MPRPRO:</b></div><hr/><i> More pure love. This is one of the most perfect B&amp;W shots I have seen on DPC. 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I love when I get to quote myself, see I told you so.<br/>This is so pretty and so artfully done even if some artsy people think it is too much or a sad statement. What we should strive for meritocracy in our photography? Please; this is, as I said, one of the most perfect B&amp;W pictures I have ever seen on DPC. It is obvious you deserved the blue.<br/> <br/>Mike<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by MPRPRO: More pure love. This is one of the most perfect B&W shots I have seen on DPC. 10   I love when I get to quote myself, see I told you so.This is so pretty and so artfully done even if some artsy people think it is too much or a sad statement. What we should strive for meritocracy in our photography? Please; this is, as I said, one of the most perfect B&W pictures I have ever seen on DPC. It is obvious you deserved the blue. Mike', '2006-01-09 15:19:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2018777, 274880, 2553, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Sorry, I really don''t mean anything against you or the model, but it does say a lot about society as a whole that a mother wouldn''t be comfortable looking as natural as possible in a moment like this.<br/> <br/>Sad really.. but that''s just one opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh my goodness!! I didn''t take offense at all!  Certainly I knew that the comments about makeup were more to the "societal" issue than the personal one!  I understand your thoughts/feelings on this as my husband feels the same way.  He would love to see all women look beautifully natural. <br/> <br/>I really appreciate all the comments!</td>', 'Originally posted by Artyste: Sorry, I really don''t mean anything against you or the model, but it does say a lot about society as a whole that a mother wouldn''t be comfortable looking as natural as possible in a moment like this. Sad really.. but that''s just one opinion.   Oh my goodness!! I didn''t take offense at all!  Certainly I knew that the comments about makeup were more to the "societal" issue than the personal one!  I understand your thoughts/feelings on this as my husband feels the same way.  He would love to see all women look beautifully natural.  I really appreciate all the comments!', '2006-01-09 15:20:41.000000', NULL, 0),
