(2026258, 274245, 42456, '<td valign="top">I think the average (commentors) had the correct opinion on this one! By the way, I gave it a ten in the voting. I''d go into all the boring reasons why...but sometimes you just have to sit back and breath the image in!! Just a wonderful job!! This one is ''All Jaxed UP''! <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-11 11:46:20.</i></td>', 'I think the average (commentors) had the correct opinion on this one! By the way, I gave it a ten in the voting. I''d go into all the boring reasons why...but sometimes you just have to sit back and breath the image in!! Just a wonderful job!! This one is ''All Jaxed UP''! ', '2006-01-11 11:44:43.000000', '2006-01-11 11:46:20.000000', 0),
(2026333, 273530, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>*Greetings from the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>Hello Anna! What a great little photo this is. There is not too much in this photo that is unpleasant to me. My only gripe would be a little more light on the left hand side of the cat. I understand though looking at this how it was taken and if you had of tried to put something there to reflect it back the cat probably would of jumped up and moved (well that''s what my cat would of done anyway). The use of the natural lighting is wonderful and your DOF sits really nicely from front to back.<br/> <br/>The tones in this picture are really good. I''m not sure if you did it PP or it was done in camera but there is some contrasting detail in the cats fur that really works well. <br/> <br/>It would of been nice to have the background laid out slightly more even. The big fold down the right hand side of it is a bit distracting. Once again I don''t know of the situation, but if the cat was already lying there and wasn''t very cooperative it would always be tricky to straighten it up without him moving.<br/> <br/>I guess the last thing I should mention is the crop. Obviously I don''t like the blown out edge on the top right of the photo. Would it have worked better with a square crop to remove that element? In my opinion I might of gone this way.<br/> <br/>Overall, this is a really sweet photo and considering your cat wasn''t cooperating and you felt rushed because of dying batteries you ended up with a nice photo. Well done!<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '*Greetings from the Critique Club*  Hello Anna! What a great little photo this is. There is not too much in this photo that is unpleasant to me. My only gripe would be a little more light on the left hand side of the cat. I understand though looking at this how it was taken and if you had of tried to put something there to reflect it back the cat probably would of jumped up and moved (well that''s what my cat would of done anyway). The use of the natural lighting is wonderful and your DOF sits really nicely from front to back. The tones in this picture are really good. I''m not sure if you did it PP or it was done in camera but there is some contrasting detail in the cats fur that really works well.  It would of been nice to have the background laid out slightly more even. The big fold down the right hand side of it is a bit distracting. Once again I don''t know of the situation, but if the cat was already lying there and wasn''t very cooperative it would always be tricky to straighten it up without him moving. I guess the last thing I should mention is the crop. Obviously I don''t like the blown out edge on the top right of the photo. Would it have worked better with a square crop to remove that element? In my opinion I might of gone this way. Overall, this is a really sweet photo and considering your cat wasn''t cooperating and you felt rushed because of dying batteries you ended up with a nice photo. Well done! Neil', '2006-01-11 12:06:49.000000', NULL, 0),
